From 985ebcb2146d65f40f59615ebecbd2ffc4c5ae3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marek 'seqre' Grzelak <git@seqre.dev>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:01:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: read the eDP link caps before setting the mode

For eDP, the sink's link capabilities are read by msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(),
called from msm_dp_display_prepare_link() in .atomic_enable(). The mode,
including the bpp, is set earlier, in .atomic_pre_enable(), and
msm_dp_panel_get_supported_bpp() limits the bpp to what fits into
num_lanes * link rate from link_info.

On the first enable after boot link_info is still zero, so no bpp fits
and the minimum of 18 is used: the panel is driven at 6 bpc although it
supports 8, and gradients show visible banding. The capabilities are read
only afterwards, and the mode keeps 18 bpp until the next full enable.

Read the eDP link capabilities at the start of .atomic_pre_enable(),
before msm_dp_display_set_mode().

Tested on an Acer Swift Go 14 AI (SFG14-01, CSOT MNE507QS2-2, 8 bpc, 4 lanes
at HBR): without this change dp_debug shows bpp = 18 after boot and 24 only
after the panel was turned off and on again.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 76aee2f..b9c3db9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -631,9 +631,6 @@ static int msm_dp_display_prepare_link(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 
 	drm_dbg_dp(dp->drm_dev, "sink_count=%d\n", dp->link->sink_count);
 
-	if (msm_dp_display->is_edp)
-		msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp);
-
 	rc = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&msm_dp_display->pdev->dev);
 	if (rc) {
 		DRM_ERROR("failed to pm_runtime_resume\n");
@@ -1430,6 +1427,13 @@ void msm_dp_display_atomic_pre_enable(struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display,
 
 	dp = container_of(msm_dp_display, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 
+	/*
+	 * eDP reads the sink's link capabilities on enable, not on HPD. Do it
+	 * here, before msm_dp_display_set_mode() picks the bpp from them.
+	 */
+	if (msm_dp_display->is_edp)
+		msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp);
+
 	crtc = drm_atomic_get_new_crtc_for_encoder(state, msm_dp_display->bridge->encoder);
 	if (!crtc)
 		return;
-- 
